// The muster at the courtyard gate (examples/captain.luau talks from this file). The captain
// asks who will speak for the company, and you answer by where you walk: options tagged
// #spot:<name> are picked by standing in that spot (a ring on the ground) for a moment or
// pressing E there, seen from above while the world slows. <<spots 12>> gives 12 seconds,
// then the #fallback option is taken: staying put is an answer too. The spots are children of
// the captain (rank, forward, ear, behind), so they go where he goes.
// Two of the ways are skill checks (#check:skill:difficulty): 2d6 plus your skill (the facts
// $skill_persuade and $skill_nerve) and any <<bonus>>, against the difficulty, the odds shown
// over the ring. Stepping past him is a red check (#red): one try, ever. While you walk he
// and his soldiers turn to watch you (<<watch Soldier*>>), and they mutter as you go: the
// Murmur nodes below are said as barks (<<barks Murmur>>), the one that fits the moment best.
// See "Story" in the scripts README.

title: Start
position: 0,0
---
<<declare $skill_persuade = 1>>
<<declare $skill_nerve = 0>>
<<call_to_order>>
Captain: Company! The gate opens at dawn, and someone speaks for us at the parley.
Captain: You there, out of the line already? Back in it. <<if not standing_at("rank")>>
<<if $read_orders>>
    <<bonus persuade 2 "You read the parley orders">>
<<endif>>
Captain: Who speaks for the company? Step up, or hold your place.
<<watch Soldier*>>
<<barks Murmur>>
<<spots 12>>
-> Hold your place in the rank #spot:rank #fallback
    <<jump Rank>>
-> Step past him and take the front #spot:forward #check:nerve:9 #red
    <<jump Forward>>
-> Lean in and whisper him an idea #spot:ear #check:persuade:8
    <<jump Whisper>>
-> Slip behind him, a hand on your knife #spot:behind
    <<jump Behind>>
===

title: Rank
position: 420,-120
---
<<set $spoke_up to false>>
Captain: Nobody. Then I speak for you, as I always have.
Captain: Dismissed.
===

title: Forward
position: 420,80
---
<<set $overstepped to true>>
<<if passed()>>
    <<set $spoke_up to true>>
    <<step_aside>>
    Captain: Bold. Then you speak at dawn, and you answer for every word.
    Captain: The company will remember who stood in front.
<<else>>
    <<set $regard_captain to -1>>
    Captain: Back in line, recruit. When I want a speaker, I will point at one.
    <<bark Laugh>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Whisper
position: 420,280
---
<<if passed()>>
    <<set $whispered to true>>
    <<nod>>
    Captain: ...Clever. Quietly now.
    Captain: If it works, it was my idea. If it fails, it was yours.
<<else>>
    <<set $whispered to false>>
    Captain: Not now, recruit. Whatever it is, it keeps until after the parley.
<<endif>>
===

title: Behind
position: 420,480
---
<<set $drew_on_captain to true>>
<<turn_around>>
Captain: I hear you, recruit. I always hear the ones behind me.
=> Captain: Put it away, and we never speak of this.
=> Captain: Again? The rest of them are watching now. <<if visited("Behind")>>
===

title: Murmur
position: 860,-120
when: moment() == "out"
---
=> Soldier 2: Where's he going?
=> Soldier 3: Here we go...
===

title: Murmur
position: 860,40
when: moment() == "near" and standing_at("forward")
---
Soldier 2: He's not serious.
Soldier 3: Somebody stop him.
===

title: Murmur
position: 860,200
when: moment() == "near" and standing_at("ear")
---
Soldier 1: What's he whispering?
===

title: Murmur
position: 860,320
when: moment() == "near" and standing_at("behind")
---
Soldier 4: Is that a knife?
===

title: Murmur
position: 860,440
when: moment() == "hurry"
---
Soldier 3: Make up your mind, green.
===

title: Laugh
position: 860,580
---
Soldier 1: Ha!
Soldier 4: Front of the line, he says.
===
